※ pl4g-test: compile=error diag=4504

※ Every turn of an ordinary loop binds a name of one type, because the loop is
※ one body run again.  A tuple's members are of whatever types they were
※ written with, so a loop over one has to be written out.

@[startup]
fn main() → u6:
    let t: 〈u8, u16〉 = 〈1u8, 2u16〉
    foreach x := t:
        0u6
    0u6
